cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Citation metadata for this software. The accompanying paper is not published
  yet, so no article reference is given here; do not cite this as a publication
  until that reference is added below.

title: "Predicted Hierarchical Action Context for Low-Level Skill Recognition in Robotic Assembly"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation for evaluating whether an online posterior over the
  parent assembly action, predicted from a three-second causal history of
  robot-state features, improves low-level robotic skill recognition on the
  REASSEMBLE dataset under leave-one-object-out cross-validation.
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/phr-devil/Hierarchical-Context-Robotic-Skill-Recognition"
url: "https://github.com/phr-devil/Hierarchical-Context-Robotic-Skill-Recognition"

# TODO(authors): replace the alias below with the confirmed author list once the
# paper's author order and affiliations are settled. Do not invent names.
authors:
  - alias: phr-devil
    website: "https://github.com/phr-devil"

keywords:
  - robotic manipulation
  - temporal action segmentation
  - hierarchical context
  - low-level skill recognition
  - force/torque sensing
  - REASSEMBLE

